From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juljus <juljus@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:54:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] fix(daemon): report a failed shell->client thread on
 every attach

When the shell->client thread of a running shell had failed, the first
attach joined it and failed with its error, which also dropped the join
handle. Every later attach took the missing handle for a live thread,
handed the client to it and failed with "sending on a disconnected
channel", so the session looked attachable but never was.

Join the thread once, keep how it ended, and refuse every attach to such
a session with the thread's error and the way out (`shpool kill`). A
thread that failed under a shell that has exited no longer fails the
attach that replaces the session.
